           }
          ],
          "text": "Topical antifungals:"
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
         "indLeft": 36,
         "indRight": 0,
         "indFirst": -18,
         "spaceBefore": 0,
         "spaceAfter": 0,
         "line": {
          "rule": "auto",
          "value": 1
         },
         "align": "left",
         "shade": null,
         "borders": null,
         "marker": null
        },
        "content": [
         {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "-    Tinea versicolor (Malassezia): topical — selenium sulfide 2.5%, zinc pyrithione, sodium sulfacetamide, ciclopirox olamine, azole (eg ketoconazole), allylamine (eg terbinafine); apply neck → knees even if lesions sm, QD x10 min (or overnight if resistant), then wash off; repeat daily x2 wk, then wkly for several months to prevent recurr"
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
         "indLeft": 36,
         "indRight": 0,
         "indFirst": -18,
         "spaceBefore": 0,
         "spaceAfter": 0,
         "line": {
          "rule": "auto",
          "value": 1
         },
         "align": "left",
         "shade": null,
         "borders": null,
         "marker": null
        },
        "content": [
         {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "-    Otomycosis (Aspergillus, Candida): ear cleaning + topical clotrimazole 1% solution BID x10–14 d; persistent → otolaryngology cleaning w/ microscopic otoscopy; refractory → oral antifungals; invasive → IV antifungals"
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
         "indLeft": 36,
         "indRight": 0,
         "indFirst": -18,
         "spaceBefore": 0,
         "spaceAfter": 0,
         "line": {
          "rule": "auto",
          "value": 1
         },
         "align": "left",
         "shade": null,
         "borders": null,
         "marker": null
        },
        "content": [
         {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "-    Oral candidiasis as a 2° infect (or bacteria): clotrimazole troches, nystatin susp, or chlorhexidine mouth rinses"
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "attrs": {
         "indLeft": 0,
         "indRight": 0,
         "indFirst": 0,
         "spaceBefore": 0,
         "spaceAfter": 0,
         "line": null,
         "align": "left",
         "shade": null,
         "borders": null,
         "marker": null
        },
        "content": [
         {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "-    Candidal balanitis: topical imidazole (clotrimazole, miconazole) or nystatin cream"
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    }
   ],
   "gap": "g_5CK6DAEJR4"
